* **Tell us about the project's reach and impact: e.g. download numbers, GitHub activity, who depends on it, or the gap it fills in the ecosystem.***
> I maintain `mcp-n8n-voice-orchestrator`, an open-source reference architecture and Model Context Protocol (MCP) bridge built for developers deploying real-time voice agents (Vapi.ai, Twilio) and WhatsApp Cloud API pipelines on top of self-hosted n8n and Supabase. 
>
> While n8n has strong general-purpose nodes, there is a major ecosystem gap when connecting Anthropic's MCP tool-calling standard to low-latency, stateful voice and messaging webhooks. Independent automation engineers and small agencies quietly rely on our blueprints and idempotency schemas to solve webhook concurrency, race conditions, and sub-second state handoffs without reinventing custom middleware from scratch. Beyond GitHub stars, our templates are actively forked and shared across developer communities by builders deploying production Claude-powered voice and messaging agents.

